Z||000000||Sootah||10-07-2001||11:37 AM||||Reupholstered... I wonder if that is even a word. Anyway, looking at an 85 GT, seats need to be re-done. How much is this going to cost me? Or should I just buy some decent seat covers? Also, the dash is cracked (its in Vegas, what do you expect?) How would I go about repairing this?<P>Havent actually seen the car yet. Leaving for Vegas in about 2 hours to look at it. This is all based on what the dude told me over the phone.<P>Peace<BR><B>-<I>Sootah</B></I><P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Sootah__Nuclear_Happy_Face_Sig.jpg">    <BR><sup><I>Never pull your pants down in Cosco, the dang monkeys will getcha</I></sup> <BR><sup><B>AIM</B>: KSSouter</sup><BR><FONT SIZE="1"><B>WANTED</B>: Aero Fiero in good condition, Manual, V6 preferred.</FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000001||sloth85GT||10-07-2001||12:18 PM||||One website that you need to visit. Do it yourself leather seat covers. If you're going to reupholster your seats, may as well go leather.<P> <A HREF="http://www.mrmikes.com" TARGET=_blank>www.mrmikes.com</A> <P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.mts.net/~kuzma/fieronl.gif">     <BR>Dan<BR>1985 Silver GT||||reg||1
Z||000002||WhiteFieroBlur||10-07-2001||02:12 PM||||Well I had a shop to my seats and I got them done in vinyl, they charged me $275 for them. They look very nice, got them done custom in black and white to go with my all black and white interior that I am about to do. Its black on the edges and white along the headrest and going down the middle. Its like top qulity vinyl and its leather looking. Can't beat that, you can have your seats anyway you want with what ever colors. I am also going to get the headliner done in black and white vinyl for about $85 dollars. But if you just have to get leather I would go with the leather, but a cheaper way would be to go with vinyl. Its just as good.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Fie Ro||10-16-2001||10:01 AM||||I have Mrmikes. I think they are the best, they fit 100%. better than most others . And you can't beat the smell of real leather ;-)<P>------------------<BR>-The Beauty & The Beast-<BR>1987 Pontiac Fiero GT & <BR>1977 Dodge W200||||reg||6
Z||000004||mshill||10-16-2001||11:27 AM||||I just picked up a mint dash for $19 at one of the four local self service junkyards.  I am going with Mr.  Mikes leather for my project and my sons 85SE restoration gets the seat covers I have been getting piece by piece from the junkyards.||||reg||1
